From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:22:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: the card 3D: frame packing says what a
 copied picture costs

Kodi of Hades 1.2.3 asks the driver for block-linear buffers that the
graphics card draws a frame-packed frame into before the dumb buffers,
and where the dumb ones are copied into by the processor it measures what
the copy of a picture costs ("copyms" in the answer of
HadesFramePackingCheck: ten black frames into a buffer that never goes
out). The card said only that the processor copies each picture; a copy
that takes longer than a picture lasts (the owner's RTX 4080 SUPER before
this: 40.45 ms at 23.976 Hz) could not be told from one that holds.

Where Kodi measured it, the card now says it after that line: "It goes
out in buffers that Hades makes in video memory. The graphics card cannot
draw into them here, so the processor copies each picture into them,
unchanged: 6.3 ms a picture." (34210, en_gb first, es_es, es_ar,
es_mx). Drawn by the graphics card, in block-linear buffers or dumb ones,
it says as before (34201); a copy without a measure, as before (34202).
The summary of a diagnostic report also names which buffers ("buffers",
"eyes") and the cost ("copyms"), only where Kodi gave them, so that the
line of an older Kodi stays as it was.
